To retrieve a previously saved game (at least in
NetHackW, the tiles version), the player has to type
in the PC name under which the game was started.

My $HACKDIR/save file, for example, contains 49
different games, each saved under a different PC
name, and to retrieve a particular one of them, I
need the PC name under which it was saved.

So the other way to ask the OP's question is: where
do save files go when the game is installed taking
all the defaults, something we won't know until we
know which OS is being considered [and which version
of NetHack, if it's a Unix-like OS, where save
directories for different NetHack instantiations can
end up in "interesting" places].

On Win32OS, a search for files whose names end in
".NetHack-saved-game" would find all the save files.

I don't know what the corresponding tag is for
Unix-likes, though.

